      source: "Engraved portrait of Moses Mendelssohn by Johann Gotthard Muller after a painting by Johann Christoph Frisch, Rijksmuseum, Amsterdam (object number RP-P-1907-2896), engraving on paper, plate 290 x 219 mm. The plate itself names the sitter (MOSES MENDELSSOHN), the painter ('p. par J.C. Frisch') and the engraver ('Grave a Stoutgard par J.G. Muller'), and carries a dedication to King Frederick William II from the Jewish Free School in Berlin dated 1787; the museum catalogues it as 1770-1775, which does not agree with the dated dedication, so the date is given here as the 1780s. It is a copy engraved after a painting, so it is a historical depiction and not a documented sitting. The image is a crop of the plate area from the museum's own image service, downscaled from about 2650 x 3650 source pixels to 870 x 1198 with no upscaling.",
