      source: "Roundel portrait from the hanging scroll 'Copy of a Portrait of Zhao Mengfu', ink and colour on silk, 63.8 x 30.8 cm, unidentified artist, 19th century, The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York (accession 1986.267.3; Gift of Robert Hatfield Ellsworth, in memory of La Ferne Hatfield Ellsworth, 1986). The museum's title names the sitter. It is a later copy of an earlier portrait, made more than five centuries after Zhao Mengfu's death, not a likeness from life. The file is a crop of the portrait roundel from the museum's Open Access image (2111 x 4000 pixels), taken at original resolution with no scaling or upscaling; the inscription and seals are cropped away.",
